# DNS Fix Guide for {{domain}}

Your domain **{{domain}}** is currently unreachable because it has no resolving DNS records (A, AAAA, or CNAME).

## Immediate Action Items

### 1. Identify Your Hosting Provider
Determine where your website is currently hosted (e.g., Vercel, Netlify, AWS, or GitHub Pages).

### 2. Update DNS Records
Log in to your DNS provider ({{dns_provider}}) and add the following records:

| Type | Name | Value | Purpose |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **A** | `@` (or leave blank) | `{{hosting_ip}}` | Points the root domain to your server |
| **CNAME** | `www` | `{{domain}}` | Redirects www to the root domain |

*Note: If you are using Vercel, the A record should point to `76.76.21.21`.*

### 3. Verify Propagation
After saving the changes, it may take up to 24-48 hours for DNS changes to propagate globally.

You can check the status using:
- [DNSChecker.org](https://dnschecker.org/#A/{{domain}})
- Command line: `dig {{domain}} A`

